# Paths excluded from VS IDE Bridge best-practice (BPxxxx) analysis.
#
# Only advisory best-practice coaching is filtered by this file. Compiler and
# language-server errors and warnings are never affected, so nothing listed here
# can hide a real defect - only a refactor suggestion.
#
# Syntax is the gitignore subset: '#' comments, '*'/'?' inside one path segment,
# '**' across segments, a trailing '/' for a whole directory, a leading '/' to
# anchor at this file's directory, and '!' to re-include. The LAST matching
# pattern wins.
#
# Inherited PrusaSlicer / Slic3r sources are included. Those files are part of
# the build, and the warnings in them show up there, so the Problems panel
# reports them too.

# --- Non-shipping trees (experiments / assets, not product ownership) --------
# Sandboxes are throwaway experiments kept for local research; shader sources
# are tabulated GPU data where renaming every float fights the medium rather
# than clarifying intent. BP here is noise, not actionable product work.
/sandboxes/
/resources/shaders/
# Localization helpers and one-off scripts (not slicer product GUI runtime).
/resources/localization/
/gcode_viewer_control.py
/scripts/
